  "result": "I fixed all three problems in `src/queue.js`, and `npm test` now passes (7 of 7).\n\n- **Hang after a failure:** a rejected job never freed its slot, so the queue stalled. A job that throws or returns a plain value, instead of a promise, is now handled too. Every job, whether it succeeds or fails, now frees its slot and lets the next job start.\n- **`onIdle()` resolving early:** it only checked that nothing was pending. It now also waits until nothing is running.\n- **Only one job after `resume()`:** `next()` started a single job per call. It now starts jobs in a loop until the slots are full, so `resume()` fills all free slots.\n\nI added five regression tests in `test/queue.test.js`:\n- a failing job rejects only its own promise and the queue keeps going\n- a synchronous throw and a plain return value are handled\n- `onIdle()` waits for running jobs\n- `onIdle()` resolves immediately when the queue is already idle\n- `resume()` with concurrency 4 and 6 queued jobs starts four\n\nI didn't check whether the new tests fail against the old code.",
